{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 40, :comments ["<b>And by your sword.</b> Like בְּחַרְבְּךָ — there are instances where עַל stands in place of בְּ, as in ״עֲמַדְתֶּם עַל חַרְבְּכֶם״ — בְּחַרְבְּכֶם; ״עַל צִבְאֹתָם״ — בְּצִבְאֹתָם." "<b>You shall break.</b> A term of distress, as in ״אָרִיד בְּשִׂיחִי״ — that is, when Israel transgresses the Torah, you will have an opening to distress him over the blessings he took. <b>And you shall break his yoke from upon your neck</b>, and so forth."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:00:50.587508430Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}